speechtext:
In so far as the Department of Industry, Trade and Commerce is concerned: 1. To date, ten orders have been placed with and announced by de Havilland of Canada, Ltd. for its DASH 7 STOL aircraft: Rocky Mountain Airways, Denver, 2; Spantax, Spain, 1;

Wardair, Edmonton, 2; Emirates Air Service, Abu Dhabi, 1; Greenlandair, Denmark, 2; Canadian Forces, 2.
2. To date, 91 firm orders have been placed with Canadair Ltd. for its Challenger aircraft and a letter of intent has been submitted by federal express of the U.S for an additional 25. The list of purchasers is extensive and has not been announced publicly by Canadair. Following normal commercial confidentiality practice, the list is held in confidence in order to preserve Canadair's competitive position.
